      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, thanks. I guess my main concern is the \"unaided memory\" part. Like, if I'm sitting there coding for a different client and I remember a specific algorithmic trick I used for this fintech firm, does that count as a \"residual\"? \n\nI want to make sure I'm not accidentally violating the NDA just by being a better developer because of the experience. Does \"unaided memory\" imply there's a specific limit to how much I can remember or use, or is it pretty much as long as I'm not looking at their actual source code?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
